<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 22 July, from 838 to 1933.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">838 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,188 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasids defeat Emperor Theophilos at the Battle of Anzen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> defeated a Byzantine army led by Emperor Theophilos at Anzen, or Dazimon, near present-day Dazman in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. In the same year the Abbasids sacked Amorion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophilos-emperor">Theophilos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1099">1099 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">927 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Godfrey of Bouillon is elected to rule Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a council in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre">Church of the Holy Sepulchre</a>, after Raymond of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> had refused the crown, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a> was elected to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. He took the title Advocate, or Defender, of the Holy Sepulchre rather than king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1209">1209 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">817 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders sack Béziers and massacre its people</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beziers">Béziers</a> and killed much of its population. A chronicler later attributed to the papal legate the words 'Kill them all; God will know his own'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1227">1227 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">799 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A north German coalition defeats Valdemar II at Bornhöved</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Bornhöved in Holstein, an army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>, Dithmarschen, Holstein and north German nobles under Count Adolf IV of Schauenburg and Holstein defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a>. Valdemar lost most of his German conquests but kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1298">1298 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">728 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward I defeats William Wallace at Falkirk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English longbowmen broke the Scottish spear formations at Falkirk, ending Wallace's career as a field commander. He was captured and executed in 1305.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1443">1443 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">583 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Schwyz and its allies defeat Zürich at St. Jakob an der Sihl</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the gates of Zürich, the confederate army led by Schwyz defeated the Zürich forces and their Austrian allies; the burgomaster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-stussi">Rudolf Stüssi</a> was killed defending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sihl">Sihl</a> bridge. The confederates then besieged Zürich.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-jakob-an-der-sihl">Battle of St. Jakob an der Sihl</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1587">1587 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">439 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John White's colonists arrive at Roanoke Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">More than 100 English settlers led by John White landed at Roanoke, intending to found the 'City of Ralegh'. When White returned in 1590 they had vanished, becoming the 'Lost Colony'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hood attacks Sherman in the Battle of Atlanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate General John Bell Hood struck Sherman's armies east of Atlanta, killing Union General James McPherson. The attack failed, and Atlanta's fall in September boosted Lincoln's re-election.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wiley Post completes the first solo flight around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wiley Post landed at Floyd Bennett Field, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, after circling the globe alone in 7 days, 18 hours and 49 minutes. An autopilot and radio direction-finder made the feat possible.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 July <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anthony-ashley-cooper-1st-earl-of-shaftesbury"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anthony-ashley-cooper-1st-earl-of-shaftesbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anthony Ashley Cooper, 1st Earl of Shaftesbury</span><span class="tp">1621–1683</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sobhuza-ii"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Sobhuza II</span><span class="tp">1899–1982</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 July <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-vii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VII of France</span><span class="tp">1403–1461</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-zapolya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Zápolya</span><span class="tp">1487–1540</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gaspar de Guzmán, Count-Duke of Olivares</span><span class="tp">1587–1645</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
